    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The «-n» rule in the plural dative",
     "texto": [
      "When we use a place preposition to say where something is in relation to several objects (plural dative), two changes are required:",
      "1. **The article:** the plural **die** becomes **den** (or with possessives: **meinen, deinen**).",
      "2. **The noun:** an **-n** is added to the end of the plural:",
      "**die Bücher** → **zwischen den Büchern** (between the books).",
      "**die Stühle** → **unter den Stühlen** (under the chairs).",
      "**die Tische** → **neben den Tischen** (next to the tables).",
      "**Exception:** If the plural already ends in **-n** or **-s**, nothing else is added:",
      "**die Taschen** (ends in -n) → **neben den Taschen**.",
      "**die Lampen** (ends in -n) → **zwischen den Lampen**.",
      "**die Handys** (ends in -s) → **auf den Handys**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
